(7713185, 1267575, 122678, '<td valign="top">One of my top pics for this challenge. Wonderful image! Super creative and really good!</td>', 'One of my top pics for this challenge. Wonderful image! Super creative and really good!', '2022-01-30 07:34:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(7713213, 1267551, 141319, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Barroness:</b></div><hr/><i> I would love to know your F stop and shutter speed. I just can''t image how you got such clarity and DOF, plus no movement of the pup. Tripod? This is a crazy good image! </i></td></tr></table>
<br/>
<br/>I shot this in a studio set up. A softbox from left top, a GoDox flash without modifiers (because I haven''t got one for the flash) from the right.  If you look closely you can see the 2 light sources in her  left eye. 

<br/>It''s the flash that created the shadows, and honestly it was a fluke. I wanted the dog to be "evenly lit", hence the 2 lights. I think I even had a white sheet on the floor as a reflector and my ceiling in the room is fairly low and also white. 

<br/>I used my 50 mm Canon lens on f 11, 1/200.</td>', 'Originally posted by Barroness: I would love to know your F stop and shutter speed. I just can''t image how you got such clarity and DOF, plus no movement of the pup. Tripod? This is a crazy good image! 

I shot this in a studio set up. A softbox from left top, a GoDox flash without modifiers (because I haven''t got one for the flash) from the right.  If you look closely you can see the 2 light sources in her  left eye. 

It''s the flash that created the shadows, and honestly it was a fluke. I wanted the dog to be "evenly lit", hence the 2 lights. I think I even had a white sheet on the floor as a reflector and my ceiling in the room is fairly low and also white. 

I used my 50 mm Canon lens on f 11, 1/200.', '2022-01-30 09:58:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(7713238, 1267575, 86447, '<td valign="top">So clever, Barbara!</td>', 'So clever, Barbara!', '2022-01-30 11:41:08.000000', NULL, 0),
